# Red Cabbage and Lentil Bowl

Based on [https://www.loveandlemons.com/buddha-bowl-recipe](https://www.loveandlemons.com/buddha-bowl-recipe) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20260130002713/https://www.loveandlemons.com/buddha-bowl-recipe/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### For the Lentils

- [ ] 1 cup [Dried Green]{ ing="dried-green" } or Brown Lentils
- [ ] 2 1/2 cups [Water or Vegetable Broth]{ ing="water-or-vegetable-broth" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [Salt]{ ing="salt" }

### For the Red Cabbage

- [ ] 2 Tbsp [Olive Oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] 1/2 head [Red Cabbage]{ ing="red-cabbage" }, thinly sliced (about 4-5 cups)
- [ ] 2 cloves [Garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [Salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [Black Pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [Balsamic Vinegar]{ ing="balsamic-vinegar" }

### For the Bowl

- [ ] 2 cups [Cooked Quinoa]{ ing="cooked-quinoa" } or Rice
- [ ] 1 large [Avocado]{ ing="avocado" }, sliced
- [ ] 1/4 cup [Hummus or Tahini Dressing]{ ing="hummus-or-tahini-dressing" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [Pumpkin Seeds]{ ing="pumpkin-seeds" } or Sunflower Seeds
- [ ] (Optional) Fresh [Lemon wedges]{ ing="lemon-wedges" } for serving
- [ ] (Optional) Fresh [Parsley or Cilantro]{ ing="parsley-or-cilantro" } for garnish

## Recipe

1. Rinse lentils and combine with water and [salt]{ ing="salt" } in a medium pot
1. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer for 20-25 minutes until tender. Drain any excess liquid
1. While lentils cook, heat [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" } in a large skillet over medium heat
1. Add sliced [red cabbage]{ ing="red-cabbage" } and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring occasionally, until softened
1. Add [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, and [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }. Cook for 1 minute
1. Stir in [balsamic vinegar]{ ing="balsamic-vinegar" } and cook for another 2 minutes. Remove from heat
1. Assemble bowls with [quinoa]{ ing="cooked-quinoa" } or rice as the base
1. Top with cooked lentils, sautéed [red cabbage]{ ing="red-cabbage" }, sliced [avocado]{ ing="avocado" }, and a dollop of hummus
1. Sprinkle with [seeds]{ ing="pumpkin-seeds" } and garnish with fresh herbs
1. Serve with [lemon wedges]{ ing="lemon-wedges" } for squeezing over the top

## Notes

- Can substitute chickpeas for lentils if preferred
- Add roasted sweet potatoes or butternut squash for extra heartiness
- Make components ahead and assemble bowls throughout the week
- For added protein, top with a fried or poached egg
- Tahini dressing recipe: Mix 1/4 cup tahini with 2 Tbsp lemon juice, 1 Tbsp maple syrup, water to thin, and salt to taste
